## Git notes

Step 1: Make sure everything is committed

On feature/authentication:

git status
Step 2: Push the latest changes
git push origin feature/authentication
Step 3: Switch to develop
git checkout develop
Step 4: Pull the latest develop

Even if you're working alone, this is a good habit.

git pull origin develop
Step 5: Merge the feature branch
git merge feature/authentication
Step 6: Push develop
git push origin develop

Now GitHub will have:

develop
Authentication ✔
Roles ✔
Permissions ✔
Users ✔
Step 7: Create a new feature branch

Never continue working on the old feature branch.

Create a fresh one:

git checkout -b feature/department-management

Then push it:

git push -u origin feature/department-management
Should we delete the old feature branch?

Yes.

Once it's merged into develop:

Delete locally:

git branch -d feature/authentication

Delete remotely:

git push origin --delete feature/authentication

This keeps the repository clean.
